<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Item&thinsp;8.01. Other Events.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Separate Trading of Class A Ordinary Shares and Warrants</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">On July 9, 2026, Yorkville
International Capital Corp. (the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;) announced that, commencing on July 13, 2026, the holders of the units issued
in its initial public offering (the &ldquo;<B>Units</B>&rdquo;), each Unit consisting of one Class A ordinary share of the Company, par
value $0.0001 per share (the &ldquo;<B>Class A Ordinary Share</B>&rdquo;), and one-third of one redeemable warrant of the Company (the
 &ldquo;<B>Warrant</B>&rdquo;), with each whole Warrant entitling the holder thereof to purchase one Class A Ordinary Share for $11.50
per share, may elect to separately trade the Class A Ordinary Shares and the Warrants included in the Units. No fractional Warrants will
be issued upon separation of the Units and only whole Warrants will trade. Any Units not separated will continue to trade on the Global
Market tier of the Nasdaq Stock Market under the symbol &ldquo;YICCU.&rdquo; The Class A Ordinary Shares and the Warrants are expected
to trade on the Global Market tier of the Nasdaq Stock Market under the symbols &ldquo;YICC&rdquo; and &ldquo;YICCW,&rdquo; respectively.
Holders of Units will need to have their brokers contact Continental Stock Transfer &amp; Trust Company, the Company&rsquo;s transfer
agent, in order to separate the Units into Class A Ordinary Shares and Warrants.</P>
